{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/677682-if-skein-astral-realms-can-changelings-enter-the-parts-not-linked-to-dreams","id":677682,"title":"If Skein = Astral Realms, can changelings enter the parts not linked to dreams?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-25T09:40:52-07:00","id":677682,"title":"If Skein = Astral Realms, can changelings enter the parts not linked to dreams?","content":"DaveB said changelings are confined to a rather limited section of the Astral. Would it step on Mages' toes if changelings could enter parts of the Astral which represent thoughts of the awake? If it is possible, how is it done? I suppose you just use the Skein Walking rules from Dancers In The Dusk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-25-2015, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:01:23-07:00","id":677742,"title":"","content":"Mages experience the Astral as four (well, kinda five actually, and you could argue making it six) layers of &quot;depth&quot; into the soul, as the souls of everything in the material world gradually combine.<br /> <br /> -Waking reality-<br /> (Meditation)<br /> Dreams<br /> The Oneiros (an individual's soul)<br /> The Temenos (Humanity's collective soul - called &quot;The Bright Dream&quot; in Beast)<br /> The Primordial Reaches (Humanity's racial subconcious - Beast's &quot;Primordial Dream&quot;. Some mages describe it as its own layer, others as the equivalent of the Gauntlet between the Temenos and Anima Mundi. Depends how much the mage knows about Beasts, really - they get to it by going right to the entrance to the Anima Mundi and then turning away.)<br /> The Anima Mundi (the planet's collective soul.)<br /> <br /> Rather than going down, Changelings skip from Dream to Dream but can't go any deeper. They can't enter the Temenos unaided because they either don't have human souls, or they're too damaged from the thorns. Take your cosmological pick. <b>Dancers</b> has changeling oneiromancers (who, despite the name, can't go into the Oneiros) accidentally summoning Oneiros beings &quot;up&quot; in to the Dream layer, and portals to the Temenos changelings simply bounce off. Maybe nonhuman beings have their own equivalents of the Oneiros and Temenos, though. Mages have observed Werewolves casually dreaming in the Anima Mundi, Beasts' Horrors pull dreamers into the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> It suits Mage to have the invisible words be ever-increasing onion layers of &quot;deeper in and further out&quot;, each bigger than the last. It suits changeling to use the metaconnections between dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-25-2015, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:40:58-07:00","id":677784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/677682-if-skein-astral-realms-can-changelings-enter-the-parts-not-linked-to-dreams?p=677742#post677742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages experience the Astral as four (well, kinda five actually, and you could argue making it six) layers of &quot;depth&quot; into the soul, as the souls of everything in the material world gradually combine.<br /> <br /> -Waking reality-<br /> (Meditation)<br /> Dreams<br /> The Oneiros (an individual's soul)<br /> The Temenos (Humanity's collective soul - called &quot;The Bright Dream&quot; in Beast)<br /> The Primordial Reaches (Humanity's racial subconcious - Beast's &quot;Primordial Dream&quot;. Some mages describe it as its own layer, others as the equivalent of the Gauntlet between the Temenos and Anima Mundi. Depends how much the mage knows about Beasts, really - they get to it by going right to the entrance to the Anima Mundi and then turning away.)<br /> The Anima Mundi (the planet's collective soul.)<br /> <br /> Rather than going down, Changelings skip from Dream to Dream but can't go any deeper. They can't enter the Temenos unaided because they either don't have human souls, or they're too damaged from the thorns. Take your cosmological pick. <b>Dancers</b> has changeling oneiromancers (who, despite the name, can't go into the Oneiros) accidentally summoning Oneiros beings &quot;up&quot; in to the Dream layer, and portals to the Temenos changelings simply bounce off. Maybe nonhuman beings have their own equivalents of the Oneiros and Temenos, though. Mages have observed Werewolves casually dreaming in the Anima Mundi, Beasts' Horrors pull dreamers into the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> It suits Mage to have the invisible words be ever-increasing onion layers of &quot;deeper in and further out&quot;, each bigger than the last. It suits changeling to use the metaconnections between dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very interesting! So, if we imagined the layers of the Astral as a wide and deep river, Mages have scuba diving equipment (and even an underwater scooter, if they are good with Mind and Space), while changelings have to jump over flotsam and toss ropes to cross said river?<br /> <br /> I wonder what features are common to the Oneiroi of Unchained. Do the props generated by their Covers extend to the inner world of their souls? Do the Unchained even have any souls of their own? Likewise, is there anything left of a Beast's Oneiros after the Homecoming/Devouring, or is it consumed by the Lair? Is the Oneiros of a Mummy significantly different from that of a mortal, beside showing abundant signs of weariness and memory holes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-25-2015, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T10:46:15-07:00","id":677785,"title":"","content":"Demons don't have souls to wander, exactly. You might fall into their Cover's Oneiros, and be decidedly disturbed at how static and frayed it can be,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:39:19-07:00","id":677926,"title":"","content":"I am not sure that I like the idea of changelings being confined to the &quot;vestibule&quot; of the Astral. Yes, they don't have human souls anymore. However, I am not certain as to what is necessary for a changeling to go &quot;downwards&quot; from the dreams layer. The first method that comes to mind is a Pledge with a Mage, or a 5 dot Contract in 2ED. Perhaps you could make the ability to travel down the Astral into a Goblin Contract, to emphasize how the changeling is not supposed to be doing that. Said Goblin Contract's Drawback could be tied to the torn souls of changelings somehow. Besides, changeling aren't just creatures of dream, they also have ties to Fate/Wyrd. Maybe sometimes they can predict just the right set of circumstances to force their way into an Oneiros, and even the Temenos or Dreamtime. They would probably have a very hard time escaping, though, and they would be somewhat out of their element.<br /> <br /> I am just suspicious that this might be going too much against the assumptions of the cosmologies in Mage or Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T14:01:33-07:00","id":677944,"title":"","content":"There's plenty to suggest that from mages point of view they deal with the Oneiros, particularly with some of the stuff from Swords and Dancers, but for Changeling's, it's all just dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T14:20:19-07:00","id":677990,"title":"","content":"MachineIV has mentioned that in 2E Changelings reach dreams by travelling through the Hedge. (I love those Goblin Miners <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Speculate away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T19:09:12-07:00","id":678397,"title":"","content":"I'd humbly suggest that the section of Swords at Dawn dealing with &quot;Dream Locales&quot; pg 117-119 would be an appropriately thematic way for a Changeling to get to the Deeper levels of the Astral Plane. Alternatively, a changeling could construct a Token, eat a Goblin Fruit, or bargain with a Morphean for the chance the opportunity. If all else fails, find a way to make the standard dream pledge with a Mage and follow them down. Pretty dangerous, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T19:35:33-07:00","id":678404,"title":"","content":"I will perhaps not as humbly suggest that, taking a step back from the in-character perspective, that the Temenos and Anima Mundi don't quite fit within the thematic and aesthetic lines of the what Changeling does. This is a pretty intimate and personal game, and the Skein model that may or may not include the Oneiros helps bring a sense of breadth by connecting people through shared experience in a way Mage's don't operate (ironically a little too individualistic there). The more mythic and esoteric reaches of the Astral, though, don't quite fit even Changeling's spiritual sense of the world or shared human experience. Hedge(heh) cases exist, of course, since weirdness and confusion is what binds nWoD's cosmology together, but to try and push for more regular access beyond the case by case needs of each individual game as might be addressed in some one off examples is to ignore how Changeling looks at that which makes up the people and the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:29:48-07:00","id":678448,"title":"","content":"There <i>is</i> no small value to the idea that Changeling does Changeling and Mage does Mage. So Changelings stay at the level of Dreams for thematic reasons. As long as they're capable of doing all the things* it's appropriate for Changelings to do in Dreams -- with all the effects* it's appropriate for those things to have -- then I don't see a problem.<br /> <br /> I mean, there certainly <i>would</i> be a problem if, say, some effect/act** that would be perfectly within Changelings' bailiwick were denied them because those things were &quot;reserved&quot; for deeper levels in Mage's model. I don't see any reason to think that's the case, though. Admittedly, I also know basically nothing of what Mages can achieve in Dreams or deeper -- to my embarrassment, I can barely remember what Changelings can do in there -- so I may not know whereof I speak.<br /> <br /> * Some of these may not be appropriate for Mages to achieve/effect unless they go deeper. Some they may not be able to bring about at all. Some of the feats both can achieve may not be stuff that Mages can manage as easily/quickly/thoroughly/etc. Just as there may be other feats it's appropriate for Mages to achieve in Dreams (or deeper) that Changelings simply can't, or can't do as easily/quickly/thoroughly/etc. They're different kinds of stories with different kinds of needs. This shouldn't really be a pissing match.***<br /> <br /> ** After considering balance concerns, not giving Changelings stuff that obviates things meant to be challenges to them, etc.<br /> <br /> *** Okay, I'll grant that I'm hopeful Changelings -- whether in general or having devoted some effort to it -- don't come off as incompetent or pushovers where dreams are concerned. It would be a bit lame to have a fair amount of value and reputation ascribed to them in that department and then just not be able to deliver at all. But I also don't really expect that to happen. Wouldn't necessarily see it as a huge deal if it did, either, depending on how it played out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:48:31-07:00","id":678464,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Dare I say?<br /> <br /> I shall simply say that I am pleased with how 2E has handled changelings as dreamwalkers. Their distinction is supported well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T21:18:04-07:00","id":678481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/677682-if-skein-astral-realms-can-changelings-enter-the-parts-not-linked-to-dreams?p=678464#post678464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shall simply say that I am pleased with how 2E has handled changelings as dreamwalkers. Their distinction is supported well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I nearly regret not being worried; had I been, that would have been very reassuring. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Great to hear, regardless!<br /> <br /> At the risk of a derail, does this come from reading their current draft, or have you had a chance to put the rules through their paces any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T22:56:22-07:00","id":678562,"title":"","content":"Reading. I'm kicking the playtests up this weekend one way or another out of a need to make good on my teasing, but one way or another, y'all should start seeing something next week.<br /> <br /> Going into a little clarity on what's been going on, there's a project I'm involved in which I thought I could get done with confidence. I mean, hell, it's <i>my wheelhouse</i>. Turns out, the entire thing's been far more obstuse than it's ever been for me, and frustratingly I've been having to push things back more and more as I deal with it-and deal with it I must, as I'm declaring it a threshold experience in my life. Monday's the cutoff date-no more time, no more rope. I'm still hammering away at it, and I expect to be done in time, but either way, done or not, this part of that project is over. If I make it, I'll still have things to do for it, but I can finally switch attention to the playtests proper. If I don't, then I can reasonably assume I'll be kicked and therefore needn't worry about it from then on, so I'll have a lot more time. Thankfully, my final semester doesn't get in the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> TL;DR, Because me and a project I'm in have been putzes to each other, it's pushed off the playtests. That's ending Monday, so the playtests'll be getting my attention correspondingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}